From 8aa04138cc4aa264174a4955a01ec2953fc6cab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Todman <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:21:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an in-game FOV slider to all four games (60-110 degrees)

Options menu of each game gains a FIELD OF VIEW slider, default 90
(vanilla). The setting lives entirely in the software renderer's
projection math, so it behaves identically on the classic renderer
and the Vulkan shader path:

- R_InitTextureMapping: at the default FOV the original expression
  and projection stay untouched (bit-identical vanilla behavior).
  Otherwise fine angles matching the user's fov span SCREENWIDTH
  and the sprite projection (walls already follow focallength)
  moves with it; out-of-range config values reset to 90.
- R_ExecuteSetViewSize: the weapon sprite scales with the same
  zoom factor so it keeps its size relative to the world.
- R_DrawPSprite: the weapon's texturemid is shifted so the texture
  row at the bottom of the view stays there (no gap above the
  status bar when the FOV widens).
- Menus: doom/strife draw the label and value with the small font
  (no M_FOV patch ships with the WADs) plus a thermometer slider;
  heretic/hexen use a text label, MN_DrTextB value and DrawSlider.
- Saved as 'fov' in the config file (range 60-110); purely a
  rendering change - demos, netgames and statdump output are
  unaffected.

Verified: 246/246 logic checks against the real finetangent table
(fov=90 bit-identical; 60-110 span correct to <0.5 deg; weapon
bottom-anchor invariant exact); quickcheck all demos byte-identical;
rendered timedemo runs at fov 60/90/110/garbage-999 produce identical
statistics (instrumented run confirms the non-default projection path
executes: 0.700 / 1.732 zoom factors at 110 / 60 degrees).
